  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Saturday)\nIssued at 129 PM MDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nWater Vapor and upper air models show upper ridge dominating the\ncentral CONUS this afternoon, with an upper low off the southwest\ncoast. Satellite shows a bit of cirrus clouds in northwestern SD,\nbut otherwise clear skies over the forecast area. Winds are light\nout of the southwest, with temperatures this afternoon in the \n70s.\n\nAforementioned upper low currently off the coast of CA is \nexpected to evolve into a wave and and move northeast early to \nmiddle of next week. Currently wave looks to move by to our south,\njust bringing some breezy winds and clouds into the forecast \narea. Expect temperatures to rollercoaster Sunday through \nThursday, but still stay at or above normal for this time of year\nand stay dry. We may see elevated fire weather conditions at\ntimes, but forecast afternoon RH's only dip into the 20-40 percent\nrange. Next chance for any meaningful precipitation comes late \nnext week. Another upper low develops off of the west coast middle\nof next week, shifting over the four corners region towards the \nweekend, and eventually sliding over the northern/central plains. \nStill far enough out that there's low confidence in timing or \nlocation of any precipitation chances.",
